y to pay for  transit to be able to get to work or to  cover rent before her paycheck comes in  it's an endless cycle it's like  being in a tornado  and you're just whirling around month  after month the high interest makes it  hard to get ahead she's been trying for  years and gaviola global news  a fire has broken out on a docked ship  that lost 40 containers off the coast of  b.c the situation on board is still  unclear but the canadian coast guard  says a safety vessel is standing by on  thursday the ship hit rough seas near  vancouver island causing dozens of cargo  containers to go overboard boaters are  being warned there's a risk of hitting  drifting cargo  still ahead the reality bending  technology that could be the future of  workspaces  [Music]  over 50 years after humans first stepped  on the moon nasa is going back the  agency will launch its orient space  shuttle in february it will orbit the  moon and then return to earth but there  won't be a crew on board nasa says it  will pave the way for a future test  flight with astronauts on board the goal  is to have boots back on the lunar  surface by 2024  back on earth a canadian aerospace  company is making giant leaps despite  being grounded by the pandemic engineers  have found a way to train astronauts in  the u.s to operate groundbreaking space  technology they've created virtual  workspaces through augmented reality  jeff sample looks at whether it's a sign  of things to come for the rest of us  for the first time since the pandemic  jessa marie zabala is back in her office  so we're right through here because of  the dreamer lab the systems engineer  works at mda for 40 years the ontario  aerospace company has trained astronauts  to operate the canadarm building five  generations of the canadian made robotic  arm used on space shuttles and the  international space station but when the  pandemic hit the team was grounded  unable to conduct its training  that is until zabala's team had an idea  that 