t it going  little amal which means hope in arabic  has traveled 8 000 kilometers to the uk  the giant puppet of a refugee girl left  turkey in july trekking across europe to  raise awareness of the difficulty  refugee children face along the way  there was a visit with the pope a strong  supporter of migrant rights  one in four canadians has symptoms of  depression anxiety or ptsd that's  according to a recent national survey a  fundraiser called ride don't hide is  raising money for people struggling with  mental health and isolation an abc man  set out on a solo ride from the 49th  parallel to the arctic ocean for the  cause as jay durant explains he says he  never felt alone  to raise money and awareness for mental  health mikey friedland decided to go for  a little bike ride his trip took him  from the canada u.s border in a soo used  to tuck the yuck duck on the arctic  ocean i didn't have any training i  planned this about three weeks before i  started and i learned as i as i went he  was on his own no car following behind  him sometimes camping at the end of the  day hello or staying in remote off the  grid cabin this is amazing  i'm in the middle of nowhere  and it is hailing on me but what makes  this adventure so special is even though  he was on his own he was never really  alone random strangers would offer him  help along the way he stopped to give me  water  and  fried chicken man some roadside meals  and snacks to help him through his ride  as i was patching my tire a man stopped  and offered me some hard-boiled eggs  friedland admits he had no idea what to  expect out there it was these  connections with the people he met that  completely  of this land i had help from dozens of  strangers  uh you know and including you know  canadians of  of of all backgrounds this is a very  narrow shoulder  after nervous moments on some highways  not very biker friendly rock slides  impeding his path  oh man  that's easy there he is bears mosquitoes  rain wind and